# Old addresses. /simulations was a page of invented Spaces; the Gallery is the one list. /play/<id> is the old play page:
# a Space's page now opens the Play chooser itself when it is asked to (?play=1).
/simulations /gallery 301
/play/:id /simulation/:id?play=1 302
# The seller dashboard moved into Projects: /creator was the list, /creator/<id> one project's selling page.
/creator /projects 301
/creator/:id /projects/:id 301

# The app's own pages. They are no files, so each is rewritten (status 200) to the app shell and the router draws it.
# The target is "/", never "/index.html": Pages redirects /index.html to / (308), and a rewrite to it answers that 308.
# Every other address that is no file and no rule here gets 404.html with a 404 status. (Cloudflare Pages serves the app shell for
# every unknown address only when the project has no 404.html.) A new route in src/app.rs needs a line here; a test checks it.
# One page per address, from a family: a Space, a marketplace item, a profile, a project's selling page, a legal act, a case.
/simulation/:id / 200
/marketplace/:id / 200
/profile/:username / 200
/projects/:sim_id / 200
/legal/:act / 200
/cases/:reference / 200
